# This crate is excluded from `aerospike-php/`'s workspace — it links the Zend API, so
# building it needs PHP headers — and therefore has its own build directory. The parent
# `.gitignore` covers `/ext/target` too; this is here so the rule survives the move to
# a standalone repository, where `ext` may not have a parent to inherit from.
/target

# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored: this crate builds a loadable
# extension rather than a library for others to depend on, so the exact
# dependency set is worth pinning.
